From d24f9dc36e5cdf4e55f069d3a554031f0ccc1010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 02:16:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Resolve a slash command whose content cannot be read

A command's `uri` is not always readable. Built-in skills are published as
discovery-only entries on the `agent-builtin` scheme that carry a name and a
description and have nothing behind them, and a file-backed command can be
deleted between discovery and use.

`resolvePromptSlashCommand` parsed that uri unconditionally, so the read
rejected and the rejection escaped the resolver. Its caller is the input
decoration update, which feeds `parsedInput`, so a message containing such a
command could never be sent and nothing was reported to the user.

Parse best-effort and make `parsedPromptFile` optional: the command still
resolves, only its body is unavailable. `promptFilePickers` already treats a
failed parse this way. Consumers skip just the part that needs a body.
