From d1035c2cf77bde3116541138800822a7208a9c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:22:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Keep cancellation and real parse failures distinguishable

Review feedback: a blanket catch also swallowed cancellation, and made a
genuine parse regression look identical to a command that legitimately has
nothing to read.

Cancellation now propagates from both resolvers, and the prompts service
traces any other failure with the command name and uri. The harness has no
logger (its constructor is not DI-decorated), so it only rethrows.

Tests cover both new branches: cancellation rejects, and a parse failure
still resolves but is traced.
